-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Move Chain Step
-- statement:
--   **Adjacent nodes of the recursive move chain are self-consistency-close.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let $\psi_{bi}$ be a bipartite state, and let `family` be an indexed polynomial family. Assume the G-hat self-consistency relation has error $2\zeta$. For every natural number $r$ and every $i\in\operatorname{Fin}(r)$, consecutive members of the recursive move-chain family satisfy
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{bi}}\left(\operatorname{Unif}(\operatorname{MoveQ}(\mathrm{params},r)),\operatorname{moveChain}(i.\operatorname{castSucc}),\operatorname{moveChain}(i.\operatorname{succ}),2\zeta\right).
--   $$
--
--   Here `moveChain` abbreviates `commuteGHalfSandwich_moveChainFamily(params,family,r)`. Each adjacent move is therefore controlled by one copy of the slice self-consistency error, which is the recursive edge input to the full move-chain composition.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_moveChain_step`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/ComparisonLemmas/CommuteGHalfSandwich/MoveChain/Chain.lean#L82-L144

